<title>AUSTRIA: SKIFLYING-RESULTS FROM WORLD CUP FIRST JUMP.</title>
<headline>SKIFLYING-RESULTS FROM WORLD CUP FIRST JUMP.</headline>
<dateline>BAD MITTERNDORF, Austria 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standings after</p>
<p>the first jump at the World Cup skiflying championships on</p>
<p>Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Takanobu Okabe (Japan) 190.2 points, 198.5 metres</p>
<p>2. Andreas Goldberger (Austria) 185.3, 191.5</p>
<p>3. Robert Meglic (Slovenia) 174.7, 183.5</p>
<p>4. Kazuyoshi Funaki (Japan) 173.7, 181.0</p>
<p>5. Primoz Peterka (Slovenia) 170.9, 179.5</p>
<p>6. Akira Higashi (Japan) 168.3, 179.0</p>
<p>7. Hiroya Saito (Japan) 167.2, 178.5</p>
<p>8. Tommy Ingebrigtsen (Norway) 167.1, 178.0</p>
<p>9. Janne Ahonen (Finland) 167.0, 177.5</p>
<p>10.Lie Haarvard (Norway) 165.6, 180.5</p>
</text>
